Technologies
ASP.NET Core Web Application (Razor Pages)/C# and Microsoft SQL Server, GitHub, Figma, and Lucidchart. 

The web application must allow users to create an account via a web interface by collecting at least the following information:
o	First name
o	Last name
o	Username
o	Phone number and/or email
o	Password
Authentication
The web application must allow a user who has an account in the application to log in only when the user provides the correct credentials.
The web application must prevent a user from logging in if the user provides incorrect credentials.
The web application must allow a user to log out of the web application.
Authorization
The web application will allow users to access a page or a feature they are authorized to.
The web application will prevent a user from accessing a page or a feature that they are not authorized to.
Administration
The web application will have at least an administrator account that has unrestricted access to every page and every feature in the application.
The web application will allow the administrator to add, edit, and/or delete a non-administrative account.
Profile Management
The web application must allow users to edit their profiles, such as their First and Last Names, Phone Numbers, Passwords, etc. 
Users can reset password via email or phone number. Users can also delete their accounts.
